.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ckman-piv-objects-export 1  ckman 
.SH NAME
ckman\-piv\-objects\-export \- Read an arbitrary PIV object
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBckman\-piv\-objects\-export\fR [\fB\-P\fR|\fB\-\-pin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIOBJECT_ID\fR> <\fIOUTPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read an arbitrary PIV object
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-pin\fR \fI<PIN>\fR
PIN code (prompted when needed)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIOBJECT_ID\fR>
Object ID as hex (e.g. 5f0000 or 5fc105)
.TP
<\fIOUTPUT\fR>
File to write the object value to (\*(Aq\-\*(Aq for stdout)
